:: The Veil [event main_quest] {"position":"3825,500","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Veil" (main_veil), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 4.2. The idea comes from The Proposition of the $prof line: I promised
   $prof.callName a unit for a whole lecture hall and told him it would take months. Now I have to build it.
   A team meeting: one unit for a whole room, the hall at the college as the first site. $brian.name wants an antenna array,
   $ethan.name loves it and names it, $darius.name asks for the raw logs and gets cleaned numbers, and writes that down.
   The quest's set unlocks project_company_veil. The router look comes later, with the gym (Gym Meeting 2). */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[15].img>><</silent>>
I've drawn it on the whiteboard before anyone comes in, because a drawing gets people arguing about the drawing instead of the idea. There's a rectangle for the lecture hall with rows of little circles for the students, and in the middle of the ceiling one box, with wavy lines coming out of it in every direction like a kid's picture of the sun.

$ethan.name is first through the door, as usual, and stops dead.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $ethan, text: "Oh, I love it already. Is it a sun? Are we going into solar?" },
{ who: $player, text: "It's not a sun. Sit down, I'll explain when everyone's here." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "Because I have opinions about solar." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

$brian.name comes in sideways behind him, sees the drawing, and his whole face changes. He doesn't even pull out a chair. He walks straight up to the whiteboard and stands there with his hands in his pockets, tilting his head at the wavy lines the way other people look at paintings.

$darius.name comes last, with a fresh notebook and a coffee he made himself, because he's tried $mom.callName's and has been polite about it ever since. He reads the whiteboard once, sits down, and opens the notebook to a clean page. He's already started a list before I've said a word.

<<linkreplace "Pitch it">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Everything we've sold so far works on a desk, for one person, maybe two, a few feet away. The official unit, $boss.callName's, the one at the diner, they're all small." },
{ who: $player, text: "So the next step is one unit for a whole room, forty people or a hundred or two hundred. You walk in and the room just feels a little nicer to be in, and nobody could tell you why." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "So, like a really good playlist, but for the air." },
{ who: $player, text: "Kind of, yeah. And I already have a first site. $prof.callName at the college wants one for his lecture hall, as a pilot study, paid for out of a research budget nobody has touched since somebody bought a smartboard." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "A pilot study, look at us. I'm going to have to start wearing a scarf indoors." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

$brian.name still hasn't turned away from the board. He lifts one hand and traces the wavy lines in the air without touching them.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $brian, text: "One emitter won't do that. Not evenly. You'd get a hot spot under the box and nothing in the back rows." },
{ who: $player, text: "So what would?" },
{ who: $brian, text: "An array. Uh, six, maybe eight small ones, phased, so they overlap. You'd have to map the room first. Walls, the ceiling height, where the bodies are. People absorb things. Like, a lot." },
{ text: "He turns around for the first time, and for once he's actually looking at me, because he's too busy thinking to remember not to." },
{ who: $brian, text: "That's a really good problem. Can I have it?" },
{ who: $player, text: "It's all yours." },
{ who: $brian, text: "Um. Okay. I'll need the floor plan. And a ladder, probably a tall one." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Let them run with it">>
For ten minutes I barely have to say anything. $brian.name draws his array next to my sun, eight neat little squares in a ring, and $ethan.name gets up to argue about the software that's supposed to keep eight emitters in step, and they disagree about everything except that it can be done. It's the best ten minutes I've had in this office. It's also exactly what I wanted to happen, which is nice.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $ethan, text: "Also, we need a name. We can't keep calling it 'the big one'. That's how you end up in an HR seminar." },
{ who: $player, text: "Go on, then. You clearly have one." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "Okay, hear me out. It goes over the whole room, it's soft, you don't really notice it, it's just sort of there, like a... veil. $company.prototype.name Veil." },
{ text: "He sits back and spreads his hands, waiting for applause. $brian.name gives him a small, serious nod, the highest honor $brian.name has." },
{ who: $player, text: "Okay, I actually like that. Veil it is." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "Write that down, $darius.name. I want it on the record that I named the thing." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

$darius.name doesn't write that down. He's been writing the whole time, slowly and evenly, and he finally lifts his pen.

<<linkreplace "Hear $darius.name out">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $darius, text: "Before we commit to a design, I'd like to understand what we're actually tuning it to, specifically how the effect decays with distance. If the official unit loses half its effect at two meters, then a lecture hall isn't simply a larger meeting room. It's a fundamentally different problem." },
{ who: $player, text: "Yeah, that's fair." },
{ who: $darius, text: "Which is why I'd like the raw logs from the diner pilot and from $boss.callName's office. The session data, every reading the units took, rather than the weekly summaries." },
{ text: "He asks it the way he asks everything, politely and precisely, as if it were the most normal request in the world, which it is, and that's the problem." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

The raw logs from $boss.callName's office would show him a curve that looks like the official unit's, because it is the official unit. The logs from the diner would show him something else: spikes on the days I sat in a booth with my coat on, my real $company.prototype.name in the inside pocket, nudging $manager.callName toward yes. Nobody looks at those days and sees a gentle product.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Sure, I'll put a dataset together for you. I'll clean it up first, though, so you've got what you need for distance and decay." },
{ who: $darius, text: "Cleaned up in what sense?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Well, they were prototypes, so a lot of the raw stuff is, you know, calibration noise, sensor drift, that kind of thing. You'd spend a week throwing out garbage, and I've already done most of that." },
{ who: $darius, text: "I don't mind throwing out garbage. Deciding what counts as garbage is most of my job." },
{ who: $player, text: "Yeah, well, this time you get to skip that part. I'll have it for you tomorrow." },
{ text: "There's a pause, short enough that $ethan.name doesn't notice it." },
{ who: $darius, text: "Tomorrow is perfectly fine. Thank you." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He writes one more line in his notebook. It's short. I'd give a lot to know what it says, and I'm not going to ask, because asking is exactly what would make it interesting to him.

<<linkreplace "Wrap it up">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "So that's the next big project. $brian.name, the array. $ethan.name, everything that keeps it in step. $darius.name, the numbers. I'll talk to $prof.callName about access to the hall." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "How long did you tell him?" },
{ who: $player, text: "I told him months." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "And how long do we actually have?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Less than that. Quite a bit less, honestly." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "Of course we do. God, I love this job." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

They leave in the order they came, and $brian.name takes a photo of the whiteboard on his way out, from three different angles, in case one of them is blurry.

I'm the last one in the room. I wipe off my sun and leave his array where it is. Then I go to my desk, pull up the diner logs, every session of every day, and start going through them one at a time, picking out the days I'd rather nobody ever saw. It takes most of the evening, and I'm still not sure I got all of them.

<<UpdateStat "+" "Morale" 3>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 1>>
<<NextQuest $player>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>
<</linkreplace>>
